      "hpi": "The longitudinal extract does not list endocarditis. Outpatient products in the extract: 24 HR metoprolol succinate 100 MG Extended Release Oral Tablet; Hydrochlorothiazide 25 MG Oral Tablet. No pre-admission creatinine was present; the first value was 1.2 mg/dL. For ten days the patient had fever, sweats, and fatigue that were new. There was no chronic febrile illness in the history obtained on arrival. Because this organism is associated with colonic lesions, gastroenterology was consulted. A colonoscopy was scheduled after the acute infection, rather than claimed as already done. Arrival temperature was 38.4 degrees Celsius. A murmur that the patient did not recognize was present. The working concern was bloodstream infection, not a finished diagnosis of endocarditis.",
